WEBVTT

00:18.702 --> 00:20.465
What are you doing?

00:21.204 --> 00:23.172
What does it look like I'm doing?

00:23.339 --> 00:25.034
I'd rather not say.

00:26.776 --> 00:28.869
I'm trying to open these cinnamon buns.

00:29.045 --> 00:31.809
- Why?
- I thought I'd try and do a little baking.

00:32.916 --> 00:34.076
Ah.

00:34.517 --> 00:35.950
You drunk?

00:36.419 --> 00:38.580
- Little bit.
- Mm.

00:40.757 --> 00:42.520
Why is it childproof?

00:43.326 --> 00:45.385
Are kids OD'ing on this stuff?

00:45.829 --> 00:47.558
Have you considered
reading the instructions?

00:47.731 --> 00:49.790
Ooh, listen to Mr. College Boy.

00:51.968 --> 00:56.029
"To open,
strike sharply on edge of counter."

00:56.206 --> 00:57.798
- Really?
- Really.

00:59.542 --> 01:01.772
All right, I'll play along.

01:03.947 --> 01:06.848
&lt;i>I christen thee HMS Kitchen Table.&lt;/i>

01:07.283 --> 01:09.114
Godspeed.

01:15.792 --> 01:17.885
I think we got a bad bun tube.

01:19.195 --> 01:20.219
Give me.

01:24.768 --> 01:26.360
Just gotta know how to whack it.

01:30.373 --> 01:33.865
I bow to your superior expertise.

01:34.878 --> 01:37.870
- So how come you're all spiffed up?
- I've got a date.

01:38.047 --> 01:40.072
Oh, two nights in a row.

01:40.250 --> 01:42.115
So who's the glutton for punishment?

01:42.285 --> 01:46.221
At the risk of tooting my own horn,
I am actually seeing two different women.

01:46.389 --> 01:48.516
- Wow, two women.
- Yeah.

01:48.691 --> 01:51.285
And yet you're still tooting
your own horn.

01:54.097 --> 01:55.155
You know what's fun?

01:55.331 --> 01:58.266
When you can talk them into tooting
each other's horns.

01:58.434 --> 02:02.427
- I'm not seeing them at the same time.
- Well, that makes it more difficult.

02:02.605 --> 02:03.936
But not impossible.

02:06.209 --> 02:09.042
You put the icing on
after it comes out of the oven, right?

02:09.212 --> 02:10.770
Right. Drizzle, don't squeeze.

02:10.947 --> 02:12.915
Thus spake the whacker.

02:16.486 --> 02:20.479
So, what prompted this break
from serial monogamy?

02:20.657 --> 02:23.125
I just got tired of putting all my eggs
in one basket.

02:23.293 --> 02:25.625
- The basket being a woman?
- Yes.

02:25.795 --> 02:27.786
And the eggs being your bun tube?

02:29.766 --> 02:33.395
No. See, the thing is, when I'm just dating
one woman at a time...

02:33.570 --> 02:35.595
- ...if she dumps me-
- When she dumps you.

02:37.073 --> 02:39.871
Either way, I have to start from scratch
finding a new woman.

02:40.043 --> 02:42.910
However, when I'm dating two women,
if one of them dumps me-

02:43.079 --> 02:44.444
When one of them dumps you.

02:45.982 --> 02:48.246
Either way, I'm not alone.

02:48.418 --> 02:49.817
Wait a second. Wait a second.

02:49.986 --> 02:52.284
You're saying
that it's advantageous to date...

02:52.455 --> 02:54.787
...more than one woman at a time?

02:54.958 --> 02:57.722
Good lord, man, you're a genius.

02:58.761 --> 03:00.092
Yeah, ha, ha.

03:00.263 --> 03:02.424
We must tell other men.

03:02.866 --> 03:06.324
- Okay, maybe I'm a little late to the party.
- A little late?

03:06.502 --> 03:10.029
The girl already jumped out of the cake
and everybody's had a piece.

03:10.206 --> 03:11.798
Well, late or not, I'm here.

03:11.975 --> 03:14.443
When it comes
to 40-year-old divorced moms...

03:14.611 --> 03:16.943
...in the San Fernando Valley,
I'm quite the catch.

03:17.113 --> 03:18.637
- I'm not surprised.
- You're not?

03:18.815 --> 03:22.649
Lights out at fat camp,
a jellybean is steak tartare.

03:23.119 --> 03:27.920
Hey, I'm- I'm single, employed,
disease-free, well-read, cute as a bug...

03:28.091 --> 03:31.424
...and perfectly capable of pretending
to like other people's children.

03:31.594 --> 03:33.585
Impressive. Did these broads know...

03:33.763 --> 03:36.698
...that you're dipping your chip
in the salsa and the guacamole?

03:37.967 --> 03:39.332
- What?
- You know.

03:39.502 --> 03:41.800
Hitting two piñatas with one stick.

03:43.039 --> 03:44.836
Topping off both tanks
with the same hose.

03:46.142 --> 03:48.508
Throwing your balls down two alleys.

03:50.179 --> 03:51.407
Still don't get it?

03:52.949 --> 03:56.248
No, I got it, and, uh- And thank you, um,
but, no, they don't know.

03:56.419 --> 04:00.014
These are divorced moms trolling for
a new schmuck to replace the old schmuck.

04:00.456 --> 04:02.651
And you let them think
that might be you?

04:02.825 --> 04:05.760
It's not like I have to lie.
Look at me, I scream schmuckdom.

04:06.996 --> 04:09.260
They're rising. It's a miracle.

04:09.732 --> 04:11.256
Yes, the miracle of yeast.

04:11.434 --> 04:12.696
I gotta go.

04:12.869 --> 04:14.131
Go, my son.

04:14.304 --> 04:18.604
Drizzle thy frosting on the divorced
sticky buns of the valley.

04:47.170 --> 04:49.604
You're a great cook, Uncle Charlie.

04:49.772 --> 04:51.034
It's no big deal.

04:51.207 --> 04:54.540
Those chefs on TV act like
they're curing leprosy or something.

04:56.980 --> 04:58.413
Can you make meatloaf?

04:58.581 --> 05:00.481
Does it come in a tube?

05:03.219 --> 05:06.245
No. God, it comes on a plate.

05:13.663 --> 05:14.755
Can I have some of that?

05:16.366 --> 05:18.664
- Beer? No.
- Why not?

05:18.835 --> 05:22.134
Because when you're 14,
you don't ask your uncle for beer.

05:22.538 --> 05:23.664
Who do I ask?

05:24.974 --> 05:27.306
I don't know.
Uh, try hanging outside a liquor store...

05:27.477 --> 05:31.004
...and look for a guy wearing house slippers
and talking to himself.

05:32.081 --> 05:33.173
What's his name?

05:39.022 --> 05:41.354
You can't have any beer, Jake.

05:41.657 --> 05:43.420
Man, I thought you were cool.

05:43.593 --> 05:45.584
I am.
And you know what makes me cool?

05:45.762 --> 05:49.027
The fact that your opinion
means less than squat to me.

05:51.534 --> 05:53.627
How old were you
when you had your first beer?

05:53.803 --> 05:56.533
Thirteen- Two. Thirty-two.

05:56.973 --> 06:00.568
- Yeah, right.
- Listen, we're talking about you.

06:00.743 --> 06:03.837
- What about me?
- Well, it's like this.

06:04.013 --> 06:07.574
Alcohol is for people
who can afford to lose a few brain cells.

06:10.686 --> 06:11.744
Yeah, so?

06:12.955 --> 06:14.081
I rest my case.

06:19.629 --> 06:20.891
What case?

06:31.607 --> 06:33.575
Morning, buddy.
How do you like your eggs?

06:33.743 --> 06:35.836
In an Easter basket.

06:38.147 --> 06:40.411
Scrambled it is.

06:40.583 --> 06:41.880
- Morning.
- Morning.

06:42.051 --> 06:43.712
- What you doing?
- Cooking breakfast.

06:43.886 --> 06:46.150
- How do you like your eggs?
- Sunny side up.

06:46.322 --> 06:47.414
Scrambled it is.

06:48.891 --> 06:50.756
&lt;i>" Cooking for Dummies "?&lt;/i>

06:50.927 --> 06:53.691
No offense, Jake.
I'm actually cooking for everybody.

06:56.833 --> 06:57.925
What brought this on?

06:58.968 --> 07:01.562
I don't know.
I thought I'd expand my horizons a bit.

07:01.771 --> 07:03.762
Uh-huh.

07:05.208 --> 07:07.199
- What?
- I'm just trying to figure out...

07:07.376 --> 07:10.345
...how scrambled eggs
are gonna get you laid.

07:11.080 --> 07:12.672
- You and me both.
- Ha.

07:15.184 --> 07:16.776
I got it.

07:18.588 --> 07:19.816
Hello?

07:19.989 --> 07:21.980
Oh. Oh, hi, Stephanie.

07:23.059 --> 07:25.960
Yeah, yeah, I, uh-
I had a great time too.

07:26.129 --> 07:28.359
Yes, it was special.

07:28.631 --> 07:30.622
Uh, I don't usually do that
on a first date either.

07:34.103 --> 07:36.537
Thank you for letting me do that,
by the way.

07:38.875 --> 07:42.402
- Uh, uh, tonight? Uh, oh, gee. Uh-
CHARLIE: Hey, Alan.

07:42.578 --> 07:44.307
- How do you like your eggs?
- Uh, uh, one sec.

07:44.480 --> 07:48.246
Um, Stephanie wants to see
me tonight, but I made a date with Katie.

07:48.417 --> 07:50.009
Scrambled it is.

07:51.754 --> 07:52.778
Um...

07:53.322 --> 07:55.950
Uh, uh, the thing is,
uh, I already made plans...

07:56.125 --> 07:59.424
...uh, with my, uh, you know, son,
who I love dearly.

07:59.996 --> 08:02.396
- What are we doing?
- Nothing. Go away.

08:03.366 --> 08:05.095
Oh, oh, what are we doing?

08:05.268 --> 08:08.066
Uh, uh, well, he and I have this, uh,
this father-son thing...

08:08.237 --> 08:09.602
...uh, where, once a week, we, uh-

08:09.772 --> 08:12.639
- Rent go-karts.
- Rent go-karts, and, uh- And, uh-

08:12.808 --> 08:14.776
- Eat pizza.
- And eat pizza. And, uh- And-

08:14.944 --> 08:16.036
- And drink beer.
- And drink-

08:16.212 --> 08:17.611
Go away.

08:18.881 --> 08:21.975
Uh, and drink, uh, a lot of water...

08:22.151 --> 08:24.346
...which the body needs to, uh,
to stay healthy.

08:24.520 --> 08:27.216
Um, anyway,
we're on for Saturday, right?

08:27.757 --> 08:30.817
Oh, okay. Uh, uh, great, great.
Good. I'll see you then.

08:30.993 --> 08:32.426
Okay, bye.

08:33.829 --> 08:36.662
- We're not going go-karting, are we?
- No.

08:37.800 --> 08:40.826
You're using me
for your own purposes, aren't you?

08:41.637 --> 08:43.366
Here's $20.

08:44.607 --> 08:46.507
Hey, Alan, taste these.

08:49.912 --> 08:51.937
Why does it smell like bourbon?

08:52.815 --> 08:55.045
The book said, "Season to taste."

08:57.987 --> 08:59.818
Just kidding, I spilled.

09:01.224 --> 09:02.248
No, thank you.

09:02.825 --> 09:03.917
Suit yourself.

09:05.428 --> 09:06.759
CHARLIE:
Hmm.

09:06.929 --> 09:09.227
A little too much egg.

09:13.269 --> 09:16.500
Jake, let's go. I told your mother
I'd have you back by 7.

09:16.672 --> 09:19.038
Hey, Alan, Alan, Alan.

09:20.876 --> 09:22.571
Would you taste
my hollandaise sauce?

09:23.312 --> 09:25.576
- You made hollandaise sauce?
- You tell me.

09:29.986 --> 09:32.011
You did not make hollandaise sauce.

09:33.456 --> 09:35.117
Damn you, eggs Benedict.

09:36.025 --> 09:37.515
Charlie, why are you doing this?

09:37.960 --> 09:40.224
- Doing what?
- In the six years I have been here...

09:40.396 --> 09:43.729
...the only time I've seen you
turn on the stove was to light a cigar.

09:44.033 --> 09:46.126
Yeah, well, people grow, people change.

09:46.302 --> 09:49.203
People get drunk
while watching the Food Network.

09:49.805 --> 09:51.466
Jake, let's go!

09:51.641 --> 09:52.903
Uh, I may not be back till late.

09:53.075 --> 09:55.407
Uh, I'm planning on giving my rose
to Bachelorette Number 2.

09:56.946 --> 10:00.973
Wow. Only you could gay up
banging two women.

10:06.355 --> 10:09.381
Says the man in the apron
with the curdled hollandaise sauce.

10:09.558 --> 10:11.924
So you admit it is hollandaise sauce.

10:12.094 --> 10:14.392
Drop me off at Gabe's house
so we can study.

10:14.563 --> 10:16.463
- Oh, you're really gonna study?
- Sure.

10:16.632 --> 10:17.656
Great.

10:17.833 --> 10:20.700
See that?
He respects me enough to lie to me.

10:21.103 --> 10:23.264
Hey, Alan, speaking of lies.

10:23.439 --> 10:26.533
At some point, one of these broads
is gonna ask you a question...

10:26.709 --> 10:28.438
...for which you will have no answer.

10:28.611 --> 10:30.340
- Like what?
- It could be as simple as:

10:30.513 --> 10:31.844
"What did you do last night?"

10:32.014 --> 10:36.075
Or as tricky as, "Why is there a pasty
stuck to your testicles?"

10:38.354 --> 10:40.515
The point is, you need to be careful.

10:40.690 --> 10:42.487
You're gonna teach me to lie to women?

10:42.658 --> 10:44.990
Well, do you know enough
to pull the pasty off...

10:45.161 --> 10:46.856
...and say, "Happy anniversary"?

10:48.898 --> 10:50.263
I do now.

10:50.433 --> 10:52.993
You need to remember:
always answer a question...

10:53.169 --> 10:54.329
...with another question.

10:54.503 --> 10:56.630
- What do you mean?
- Exactly.

10:57.840 --> 10:59.501
- What?
- Great, you're all set.

11:01.177 --> 11:02.371
- Drunk again?
- Yep.

11:04.380 --> 11:05.404
Well, uh, thank you.

11:05.581 --> 11:07.606
- Uh, I appreciate the advice.
- I've got more.

11:07.783 --> 11:09.978
Uh, Charlie, please don't take this
the wrong way...

11:10.152 --> 11:12.620
...but if a semi-functioning wino
such as yourself...

11:12.788 --> 11:17.122
...can date several women at the same time,
I'm quite certain I can handle two.

11:20.196 --> 11:22.289
Why would I take that the wrong way?

11:25.000 --> 11:28.902
Ugh. Tastes like stale ass.

11:33.442 --> 11:38.004
Mm. Oh. Is it just me, or does this thing
we have feel really, really comfortable?

11:38.180 --> 11:39.545
- Oh, yeah.
- Ha, ha.

11:39.715 --> 11:42.445
I mean, you know, maybe not
pet-names-for-our-pee-parts comfortable...

11:42.618 --> 11:44.279
...but, uh, we're certainly getting there.

11:46.188 --> 11:50.989
Oh, hey, next week, my ex is taking
my daughter to see his parents...

11:51.160 --> 11:54.186
...so you and I can spend
the whole weekend in bed.

11:55.564 --> 11:56.792
That sounds great.

11:56.966 --> 11:58.297
I'll leave myself alone till then.

12:01.937 --> 12:03.029
Oh, oh, oh. Wait, wait.

12:03.205 --> 12:05.673
Uh- Uh, uh, next weekend?

12:05.841 --> 12:08.401
Ahh, uh, you know, ah,
I'll have to check...

12:08.577 --> 12:10.977
...but I think Saturday is, uh...

12:11.147 --> 12:13.081
...a working Saturday for me.

12:13.249 --> 12:14.614
Oh, no, really?

12:14.784 --> 12:17.514
Yeah, yeah. It's unfortunate,
but in today's economic climate...

12:17.686 --> 12:21.645
...uh, Saturday is no longer the Sabbath
for anybody, except religious Jewish people.

12:21.824 --> 12:24.156
You know, the guys with the beards
and the hats.

12:24.326 --> 12:28.194
&lt;i>Uh, did you see Yentl? I love that movie.
That's one I wouldn't mind owning.&lt;/i>

12:29.899 --> 12:31.764
Alan, are you seeing another woman?

12:34.203 --> 12:36.933
Charlie, are you seeing another woman?

12:37.106 --> 12:38.630
Why would you ask me that?

12:39.074 --> 12:41.599
I just need to know I can trust you.

12:41.777 --> 12:44.371
Yeah, well, trust is a two-way street.

12:44.847 --> 12:47.441
- I know.
- Do you?

12:47.616 --> 12:51.143
Because without trust,
all we have is sex.

12:53.155 --> 12:54.986
Well, you can trust me, Charlie.

12:55.157 --> 12:56.818
God, I hope so.

12:56.992 --> 12:58.391
I've been hurt before.

12:59.662 --> 13:03.723
Aw. Well, I won't hurt you. I promise.

13:03.899 --> 13:05.890
Okay, then.

13:08.938 --> 13:10.997
- Another woman?
- Yeah.

13:11.173 --> 13:12.970
Well, uh- Oh, you think I'm involved...

13:13.142 --> 13:15.007
- ...with another woman? Heh.
- Yeah.

13:15.177 --> 13:17.202
You actually think
I'm seeing someone else...

13:17.379 --> 13:19.472
- ...at the same time I'm seeing you?
- Yeah.

13:19.648 --> 13:21.343
How did you know?

13:25.588 --> 13:26.953
Uh, do you need to get that?

13:27.122 --> 13:29.386
- Are you crazy?
- Mm. Ha.

13:29.558 --> 13:31.082
&lt;i>CHARLIE
Hey, it's Charlie.&lt;/i>

13:31.260 --> 13:33.319
&lt;i>Do your thing when you hear the beep.&lt;/i>

13:35.130 --> 13:37.325
&lt;i>JAKE: Hey, Uncle Charlie, it's me, Jakey.&lt;/i>

13:37.500 --> 13:38.933
&lt;i>I'm drunk. How are you?&lt;/i>

13:40.636 --> 13:44.402
&lt;i>Are you with a girl?
Does she have big ones?&lt;/i>

13:45.107 --> 13:46.369
Jake, where are you?

13:48.143 --> 13:49.838
What mall?

13:50.713 --> 13:53.807
They all have pretzel stands, you doofus.

13:55.484 --> 13:58.851
Okay, you stay right where you are,
and I'll come get you.

13:59.822 --> 14:01.119
We'll talk about that later.

14:02.691 --> 14:04.454
They're big enough.

14:06.562 --> 14:08.496
I love you too, buddy.

14:09.431 --> 14:10.955
Yeah, we have shared
some good memories.

14:13.102 --> 14:15.798
Okay, I'm hanging up now.

14:16.472 --> 14:18.303
Do you have to go?

14:19.608 --> 14:21.473
No, we got time.

14:28.183 --> 14:30.674
What the heck took you so long?

14:30.853 --> 14:33.720
Believe me, I came as quickly as I could.

14:34.189 --> 14:35.451
What the hell is that?

14:35.624 --> 14:38.787
- Soft pretzel. You want some?
- No, thanks.

14:39.228 --> 14:41.128
It's got jalapeños.

14:41.564 --> 14:42.826
You're gonna regret that.

14:43.332 --> 14:45.698
- What do you mean?
- You'll see.

14:45.868 --> 14:47.358
Where'd you get the booze?

14:47.536 --> 14:48.935
I did what you told me to do.

14:49.104 --> 14:51.971
Me and Gabe gave money
to a creepy guy to buy us beer.

14:52.141 --> 14:53.199
Oh, Jake.

14:53.375 --> 14:55.741
His name was Satellite Jack.

14:55.911 --> 14:57.970
He said the government
stole his kidneys.

14:58.914 --> 15:01.212
Is $20 too much for a six-pack?

15:01.850 --> 15:05.877
Not when a guy with no kidneys
named Satellite Jack is buying it for you.

15:06.155 --> 15:07.645
Where'd you get the $20?

15:07.823 --> 15:10.189
- It was a bribe from my father.
- You're kidding.

15:10.359 --> 15:13.624
I know. For a cheap guy,
he can be surprisingly generous.

15:14.763 --> 15:15.787
That's true.

15:16.298 --> 15:18.698
Deep down, I love him.

15:19.702 --> 15:22.227
And I love you too.

15:22.404 --> 15:25.669
Great, great. Everybody loves everybody.

15:26.342 --> 15:27.570
So where's your friend?

15:27.743 --> 15:32.237
Gabe? He ditched me when I started
throwing up. The bat rastard.

15:33.048 --> 15:34.345
- Get out of the car.
- What?

15:34.516 --> 15:36.484
I just had it detailed. Get out, get out.

15:36.652 --> 15:39.485
All right, but I'm telling you,
I'm all done throwing up.

15:41.890 --> 15:45.587
Ugh, I see what you mean
about those jalapeños.

15:46.895 --> 15:49.489
My mom still thinks
I'm studying at Gabe's house...

15:49.665 --> 15:52.759
...so I don't think I should go home
at this time.

15:52.935 --> 15:54.664
Well, what do you expect to do?

15:54.837 --> 15:57.772
I don't know.
You up for an R-rated movie?

15:58.207 --> 16:00.641
Boobies, no violence.

16:02.711 --> 16:03.735
Uh-oh.

16:03.912 --> 16:05.243
Step away from the car.

16:06.815 --> 16:09.648
- Nope, false alarm.
- Wait for it.

16:09.818 --> 16:10.842
Wait for what?

16:13.222 --> 16:15.713
Oh, how about that?

16:16.258 --> 16:19.159
- You get any on your shoes?
- A little.

16:21.463 --> 16:23.226
There's a plastic bag in the trunk.

16:23.399 --> 16:25.629
Remove your shoes
and place them in the bag...

16:25.801 --> 16:28.167
...then seal it
and put it back in the trunk.

16:28.337 --> 16:29.702
Okay.

16:29.872 --> 16:31.237
Then climb in after it.

16:31.407 --> 16:32.965
Okay.

16:48.390 --> 16:50.483
- Alan.
- Surprise. Ha, ha.

16:50.659 --> 16:52.718
I thought you were
with your son, go-karting.

16:53.195 --> 16:55.527
Yeah, uh, listen, um...

16:55.698 --> 16:56.756
...I lied about that.

16:56.932 --> 16:58.991
But, you know, I can't lie anymore.

16:59.168 --> 17:03.195
I was with another woman,
but all I could think about was you.

17:03.372 --> 17:07.638
I'm a one-woman man,
and, baby, you're that woman.

17:08.277 --> 17:10.575
Who is it, honey?
- Just a salesman.

17:10.746 --> 17:11.872
Go away.

17:12.047 --> 17:13.912
- Are you seeing someone else?
- Get lost.

17:14.083 --> 17:17.177
But I thought we had something special.

17:17.352 --> 17:20.253
Who's in there? Are you married?
Because I really thought I-

17:45.614 --> 17:48.378
You know,
your body's sending you a message.

17:48.550 --> 17:51.713
Yeah, it's saying I should really
chew my food more.

17:52.588 --> 17:55.921
Look at that shrimp.
You could wash it off and serve it again.

17:57.192 --> 17:59.990
Your body is also telling you
that alcohol is poison.

18:00.162 --> 18:02.460
If it's poison, why do you drink it?

18:02.631 --> 18:06.226
Because there are things inside of me
I need to kill.

18:06.769 --> 18:08.760
You can't kill bad feelings with alcohol...

18:08.937 --> 18:11.030
- ...Uncle Charlie.
- Right.

18:11.206 --> 18:13.401
And you can't stuff your emotions
with cupcakes.

18:13.575 --> 18:15.338
Believe me, I've tried.

18:15.511 --> 18:17.069
I'm sure you have.

18:17.246 --> 18:19.874
If you ever need to talk
about any of this stuff, I'm here for you.

18:22.351 --> 18:23.818
Good to know.

18:23.986 --> 18:27.114
Whoa, I felt that one in my nuts.

18:27.723 --> 18:30.157
Hello? Anybody home?

18:30.325 --> 18:31.656
Are you gonna rat me out?

18:31.827 --> 18:34.489
Jake, buddy,
how could you even ask me that?

18:43.839 --> 18:46.171
Hey, what's going on?

18:47.176 --> 18:50.668
Jake took the 20 bucks you gave him
and got drunk with a friend.

18:54.850 --> 18:56.078
Oh.

18:57.386 --> 18:59.718
Bad boy.

19:08.931 --> 19:11.331
So how about a beer?

19:23.378 --> 19:26.108
Never again.

19:27.015 --> 19:28.915
Me neither.

19:30.986 --> 19:32.510
You know what the problem is?

19:32.688 --> 19:34.519
The women, the drinking?

19:34.990 --> 19:37.550
You guys look at me
and you think it's easy.

19:38.026 --> 19:41.518
What you don't see is all the years
of hard work and dedication it took...

19:41.697 --> 19:45.326
...to make me the happy-go-lucky
drunken ass-wrangler I am today.

19:47.302 --> 19:48.701
INGRID:
Charlie?

19:48.871 --> 19:51.362
Oh, sorry, baby.
I had a little family drama.

19:51.540 --> 19:53.974
Remember, you said
if I gave you what you want...

19:54.142 --> 19:55.905
...you'd give me what I want.

19:56.078 --> 19:58.376
Right, breakfast in bed.

19:59.748 --> 20:02.114
- How do you like your eggs?
- Scrambled.

20:02.818 --> 20:04.376
Yes.

20:09.625 --> 20:12.150
You know, young man...

20:12.594 --> 20:17.031
...if I hadn't had been electrocuted
earlier this evening...

20:17.199 --> 20:20.965
...you and I'd be having a serious talk
right now.

20:21.737 --> 20:24.069
Yeah, hold on.
